  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0 -- AI settings moved from appsettings.json to the database. Providers and API keys now live in the WA_AiSettings table (created automatically at startup on SQL Server and PostgreSQL), not in the Ai:Chat / Ai:Embedding sections. Each role (Chat, Embedding, or an app-defined role such as Interviewer) can have any number of providers, tried in ascending Priority: on a 429 (free quota used up), timeout, 5xx or revoked key the call moves on to the next provider (streaming: only before the first token; embeddings: only to providers with the same Model and Dimensions). API keys are stored encrypted: AES-256-GCM with the Ai:EncryptionKey setting (portable across servers), or ASP.NET Core Data Protection when it is not set; a plaintext key typed in the form or directly in the table is encrypted automatically. New: AiClients (GetChatClient(role) / GetEmbeddingGenerator(role)), AiSettingsService, AiSecretProtector, WaUiOptions.AiSettingsImport; IChatClient / IEmbeddingGenerator in DI are now the Chat / Embedding roles with failover. Migration: the old Ai:Chat / Ai:Embedding sections (single object or array) are imported once at startup, then remove them from appsettings and rotate the keys. Behaviour change: AI is on when Ai:Enabled is not false and the role has a usable provider (it used to be off when Ai:Enabled was missing). Removed: AiClientFactory.CreateChatClient(IConfiguration) / CreateEmbeddingGenerator(IConfiguration) (now take one provider row). Admin screen: copy FM _DATA/WA_AiSettings + the WA_AiSettings profile node (see AI_SETTINGS.md in the source repository). Also: Data Management -- Table Designer, settings.xml designer and table settings dialog.",
